# Rust / Tauri
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# The bundled GnuPG (ADR-14). Fetched by `scripts/fetch-gnupg.sh` at build time
# and never committed: it is a third-party binary tree with its own release
# cadence, and the checksum in the script is what makes it reproducible. The
# directory itself is kept so `bundle.resources` always resolves — on Linux,
# which is not bundled for, it stays empty.
src-tauri/gnupg/*
!src-tauri/gnupg/.gitkeep
!src-tauri/gnupg/README.md

# Never commit secrets, keys, or a real store (PLAN.md §9).
# Integration tests build their store and GNUPGHOME at runtime (PLAN.md §8),
# so nothing encrypted should ever need to be checked in.
.env
.env.*
*.gpg
*.asc
*.key
.gpg-id
.password-store/
.gnupg/

